From 13adbcc3eacdb5eca7cd41d0c6810b32ed0fbe11 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: FiyeroT <me@fiyero.xyz>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 09:39:26 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 144/147] domainset: ReadSourceAddresses reads a rule set
 without building its names

For those who want the addresses of a rule set of the source format and
the shape of its rules, not its matcher (the Go backend of podkop makes
the sets of its firewall of them): the names of domain and domain_suffix
are counted and the first three of each kept as the lists of the rule,
the trie is not built. Everything else is read as ReadSource reads it.
A list of 300000 names: 6 ms and under 1 KB, against 72 ms and 22 MB.
---
 common/domainset/addresses_test.go | 79 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 common/domainset/source.go         | 72 +++++++++++++++++++++++----
 2 files changed, 141 insertions(+), 10 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 common/domainset/addresses_test.go

